full_text:
Due to Hurricane Irene, parts of New Jersey were declared a federal disaster area this week. Federal funding is available  to residents and businesses affected by the storm, according to the New Jersey Office of Emergency Management (OEM).
Eligible activities for individual assistance include:
Damage to or destruction of real property, including primary residences, dwellings, buildings, and structures;
Permanent losses, including contents, and personal property;
Displacement and relocation expenses, including temporary housing;
Other necessary expenses or serious economic hardship, including medical expenses and funeral expenses.
Eligible businesses can apply for disaster loans to cover:
Physical damage to real property, machinery, and equipment;
Economic losses, including inventory and supplies;
Working capital needs to ensure continued operations.
To

